; negative case for `thus` (see thus.kurt for the positive case): the last line of the proof
; is not literally the planned goal, even though the goal is still derivable from it in one
; more step -- `thus` rejects this, unlike `qed`, which would happily search for that step.
;
; note: this can't use `expect` (see forall-intro-rejects-leaked-constant.kurt for the same
; reasoning) -- the failure happens while `thus` itself closes the `proof` block, not while
; evaluating an ordinary statement inside it; hence the older `;;; ` marker convention here.
load prop
bool A, B, C
use A implies B
use B implies C
use A

show C
proof
    B
thus
;;; ProofError: last formula `B` is not literally the planned formula `C`
